solution:
System is in a closed container. So there will be no heat transfer. Therefore the heat is $q=0$. Now liquid is stirred with a paddle to increase the temperature which increases the internal energy $\Delta E$ of the system.<br/>$$<br/> egin{aligned}<br/>&amp; \Delta \mathrm{E}=n \mathrm{C} \Delta \mathrm{T} \<br/>&amp; \Delta \mathrm{E} 
eq 0<br/>\end{aligned}<br/>$$<br/>Work is also done on the system when started with a paddle.<br/>$$<br/> egin{gathered}<br/>\mathrm{W} 
eq 0 \<br/>\Delta \mathrm{E}=q+\mathrm{W}=0+\mathrm{W}, \Delta \mathrm{E}=\mathrm{W} \<br/>\Delta \mathrm{E}=\Delta \mathrm{W} 
eq 0, q=0<br/>\end{gathered}<br/>$$

